---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const updated = '23 June 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Asteris Commerce"
  description="How Asteris Commerce (My Cosmic Message Pty Ltd) collects, uses, and protects personal information across asteriscommerce.com, the purchase and licensing flow, and the Asteris plugins. Australian Privacy Act 1988 / APPs, with GDPR and CCPA notes."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        How we collect, use, and protect personal information across this website, our
        purchase and licensing system, and the Asteris plugins. We collect the minimum we
        need, and we never sell your data.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-06-23">{updated}</time></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="body">
    <div class="container">

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This website (<strong>asteriscommerce.com</strong>) and the Asteris range of products
        are operated by <strong>My Cosmic Message Pty Ltd</strong>, trading as
        <strong>Asteris Commerce</strong> — an Australian proprietary limited company
        (ACN 652 358 159, ABN 30 652 358 159), registered in New South Wales, Australia. In
        this policy, "we", "us", and "our" refer to My Cosmic Message Pty Ltd.
      </p>
      <p>
        For any privacy question or request, contact
        <a href="mailto:support@asteriscommerce.com">support@asteriscommerce.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Scope</h2>
      <p>This policy covers three distinct contexts, which we treat differently:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>This website</strong> — what we collect when you browse asteriscommerce.com and our related product sites.</li>
        <li><strong>Purchases &amp; licensing</strong> — what we collect when you buy a licence and how we manage it.</li>
        <li><strong>The Asteris plugins</strong> — software you install on your own WordPress site. Because the plugins run on <em>your</em> server, your store and customer data stays with you. See section 8.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Information we collect</h2>
      <p><strong>When you browse this website:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Analytics data</strong> via Google Analytics 4 — pages viewed, approximate location (derived from IP, which Google truncates), device and browser type, referral source, and on-site behaviour. This is used in aggregate to understand and improve the site.</li>
        <li><strong>A consent-preference cookie</strong> (set in your browser's local storage) recording whether you accepted or declined optional cookies.</li>
        <li><strong>A partner referral identifier</strong> — if you arrive via a partner link (<code>?ref=</code>), we store that reference in your browser and pass it through to checkout so the partner is credited.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>When you buy a licence:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your <strong>name and email address</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Billing details</strong> needed to complete the transaction. Payments are processed by <strong>Stripe</strong> — we never see or store your full card number, CVC, or banking credentials.</li>
        <li><strong>Licence and activation data</strong> — your licence key(s), the website URL(s) where a licence is activated, product and version, and activation status. This is how updates and support are delivered to paying customers.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>When you contact us:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your email address and the content of your message, so we can respond and keep a support history.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. How we use your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To deliver licences, software updates, and customer support.</li>
        <li>To process payments, renewals, and refunds.</li>
        <li>To operate the partner/affiliate program (crediting referrals).</li>
        <li>To understand and improve our website and products (aggregate analytics).</li>
        <li>To detect, prevent, and address fraud, abuse, or security issues.</li>
        <li>To send transactional emails (receipts, licence keys, renewal and expiry notices). We do not send marketing email without your consent.</li>
        <li>To comply with legal, tax, and accounting obligations.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We rely on the lawful bases of <strong>contract</strong> (to provide what you bought),
        <strong>legitimate interests</strong> (to run and secure the business), <strong>consent</strong>
        (optional analytics cookies), and <strong>legal obligation</strong> (tax records).
      </p>

      <h2>5. Cookies &amp; tracking</h2>
      <p>
        We use a small number of cookies and browser-storage items: Google Analytics 4 cookies
        (analytics), a consent-preference item, and, where applicable, a partner-referral item.
        You can accept or decline optional cookies via the banner shown on your first visit, and
        you can clear them at any time through your browser settings. Declining does not affect
        your ability to browse or purchase. We do not use advertising cookies or cross-site
        behavioural tracking.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information. We share it only with the
        service providers needed to run the business, each acting under their own privacy and
        security obligations:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — payment processing.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — website analytics.</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — content delivery and security.</li>
        <li><strong>Our hosting and email providers</strong> — to host pay.asteriscommerce.com (our licensing system) and to send transactional email.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may also disclose information where required by law, or to protect our rights, users,
        or the public.
      </p>

      <h2>7. International data transfers</h2>
      <p>
        We are based in Australia, and some of our service providers process data in other
        countries (for example, the United States and the European Union). Where personal data
        is transferred internationally, we rely on the safeguards and contractual protections
        offered by those providers.
      </p>

      <h2>8. The Asteris plugins and your customers' data</h2>
      <p>
        The Asteris plugins are <strong>self-hosted software</strong> that you install on your own
        WordPress site. They are not a cloud service. Any merchant or customer data the plugins
        process is stored in <em>your</em> WordPress database, on <em>your</em> host — we do not
        receive it.
      </p>
      <p>Some features make outbound calls to third-party services, and only when you use that feature:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Licence verification</strong> (paid editions) — sends the site URL and licence key to pay.asteriscommerce.com to validate the licence and deliver updates.</li>
        <li><strong>Business-number validation</strong> — Australian ABN lookups via the Australian Business Register (ABR); EU VAT lookups via the European Commission's VIES service.</li>
        <li><strong>SEO and AI features</strong> — keyword and SERP data via DataForSEO; AI generation via your chosen AI provider using your own API key.</li>
        <li><strong>Payouts</strong> (affiliate features) — via Stripe or PayPal where you enable them.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Each plugin documents the external services it uses in its readme. <strong>Free editions
        published on WordPress.org make no external calls beyond the documented services above.</strong>
        As the site owner, you are the data controller for your store and customer data, and you
        are responsible for your own privacy disclosures to your customers.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep purchase, licence, and tax records for as long as required to provide the service
        and to meet Australian legal and accounting obligations (generally a minimum of five
        years for financial records). Support correspondence is kept while it remains useful for
        servicing your account. Analytics data is retained per Google Analytics' configured
        retention period. We delete or anonymise data when it is no longer needed.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect personal information,
        including encryption in transit (HTTPS), restricted access to systems, and reputable
        infrastructure providers. No method of transmission or storage is perfectly secure, but
        we work to protect your data and to respond promptly to any incident.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the Australian Privacy Act 1988 and the Australian Privacy Principles — and, where
        applicable, the EU/UK GDPR and the California Consumer Privacy Act — you may have the right
        to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access the personal information we hold about you.</li>
        <li>Request correction of inaccurate information.</li>
        <li>Request deletion of your information, subject to our legal retention obligations.</li>
        <li>Object to or restrict certain processing, and withdraw consent for optional cookies.</li>
        <li>Request a copy of your data in a portable format.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise any of these, email <a href="mailto:support@asteriscommerce.com">support@asteriscommerce.com</a>.
        We will respond within a reasonable time and may need to verify your identity first.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Children</h2>
      <p>
        Our website and products are intended for businesses and adults. We do not knowingly
        collect personal information from children under 16.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top reflects
        the latest version. Material changes will be made prominent on this page.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Contact &amp; complaints</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, requests, or complaints:
        <a href="mailto:support@asteriscommerce.com">support@asteriscommerce.com</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Legal entity:</strong> My Cosmic Message Pty Ltd t/a Asteris Commerce,
        ACN 652 358 159, ABN 30 652 358 159, Sydney, NSW, Australia.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are in Australia and are not satisfied with our response, you may contact the
        Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC) at
        <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" target="_blank" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>See also</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a></li>
        <li><a href="/about">About Asteris Commerce</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding: 80px 0 24px; }
  h1 {
    font-size: 64px;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -2px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .lead { font-size: 22px; color: var(--c-muted); max-width: 760px; }
  .updated { font-size: 16px; color: #888; margin-top: 16px; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { h1 { font-size: 40px; } }

  .body { padding: 24px 0 80px; }
  .body :global(h2) {
    font-size: 26px;
    margin: 36px 0 12px;
    color: var(--c-black);
  }
  .body p {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #333;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .body p strong { color: var(--c-black); }
  .body code {
    background: #f2f2f2;
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }
  .body ul {
    margin: 0 0 18px 22px;
    color: #333;
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .body ul li {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .body a { color: var(--c-orange); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .body a:hover { color: var(--c-black); }
</style>
